From: David Freeman <david@tinytrashlabs.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 22:44:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] =?UTF-8?q?refactor(app):=20per-backend=20license=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?acks=20=E2=80=94=20Fish=20and=20SuperTonic=20are=20distinct=20l?=
 =?UTF-8?q?icenses?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the Fish-only didAckFishLicense bool with ackedLicenses:
Set<BackendID> (persisted as a sorted string array under
'ackedLicenses'), didAck(_:), and ackLicense(_:) which persists AND
tells the engine. Every needsLicenseAck gate (backend didSet, generate,
loadModel, synthesizeLine, bakeExpressionVariants, chat regenerate,
Settings rows) now checks the backend actually being used, so acking
Fish (research/personal) never unlocks SuperTonic (Open RAIL-M) or
vice versa.

Migration: on load, a true legacy 'didAckFishLicense' seeds {fishS2Pro}
so existing users are never re-prompted; init re-acks every persisted
backend with the engine (was Fish-only).

FishLicenseSheet becomes LicenseSheet: title + notice come from the
pending backend via StudioKit's licenseNotice(for:), confirm wording is
now the license-neutral 'I Agree to the Use Restrictions'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
